{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/bpy.app Module.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/bpy.app Module.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bpy.app module bpy.app module","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/bpy.app Module.md","fileName":"bpy.app Module.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"bpy.app Module","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Python Data and Operations]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Python Data and Operations","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/bpy.app Module.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/bpy.app Module.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bpy.app module bpy.app module","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/bpy.app Module.md","fileName":"bpy.app Module.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"bpy.app Module","heading":"bpy.app Module","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"`bpy.app` exposes information and services belonging to the running Blender application rather than to a single scene object. Of particular importance, `bpy.app.handlers` stores lists of functions that Blender calls around events such as frame changes, rendering, loading, and saving.\n\nApplication handlers make scripts reactive instead of purely sequential. A function can update data before a scene refresh or run diagnostics after a file loads. Because these hooks outlive the immediate statement that installed them, their creation, removal, and persistence need deliberate lifecycle management.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Python Data and Operations","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/bpy.app Module.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/bpy.app Module.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bpy.app modul